      "question": "What changes if finding a promising material takes less time than independently testing it?",
      "baseline": "The 1990 book already anticipated an age of biology. A different proposition is that computational tools could help researchers move repeatedly between a question, a proposed design and a real-world test. McKinsey added AI for scientific discovery and engineering as a distinct domain in 2026.",
      "implication": "Materials, medicines and manufacturing processes could develop on shorter cycles. Access to facilities, data and independent validation would shape whose problems attract attention.",
