      "title": "Economic and political activity expands into orbit",
      "question": "How might everyday services change when their communications, navigation or observations depend on decisions made about orbital infrastructure?",
      "baseline": "Weather forecasting and navigation already depend on space. The candidate shift is satellite services becoming everyday dependencies for more sectors while commercial providers and states negotiate access, spectrum and the use of shared orbital space.",
